[09:18:29] assistant
Khanmigo: Socratic-only, refuses direct answers. Strong pedagogically but users report frustration —
          sometimes you just need the answer to move forward. LearnLM: Google's fine-tuned model for
          learning contexts, better at pedagogical framing, but generic. Neither integrates with the
          student's actual course material. That's the real gap — both are general tutors. Neither
          knows what the student studied this week, in this course, up to this specific moment.

